    <!-- TO RELEASE, two steps:

           mvn clean install                                        <- builds all modules, runs the tests
           mvn clean deploy -P release -pl docx4j-ImportXHTML-core  <- publishes -core only

         Both steps are needed.  -core has no src/test of its own: the whole suite lives in
         -core-tests, which -pl excludes, so the deploy step on its own runs no tests at all.
         Do the install first and check it is green.

         Don't try to fold the two together with -pl docx4j-ImportXHTML-core,docx4j-ImportXHTML-core-tests:
         that runs the tests, but -core-tests is then last in the reactor, which breaks the
         upload for the reason set out below.

         Only -core goes to Maven Central.  Since 17.0.2 we no longer publish the parent
         either; the poms we publish are flattened and carry no <parent>, so consumers
         never resolve it.

         The -pl is what keeps it to -core, and there is no way to get the same result from
         configuration alone.  Both alternatives are wrong, in opposite directions:

         Run "mvn clean deploy -P release" as it stands, and you publish the parent and
         -samples as well as -core.  Only -core-tests stays out, that being the one module
         with skipNexusStagingDeployMojo actually in effect (in -samples the same block is
         inside a TODO comment, deliberately - see below).

         Uncomment it in -samples, though, and you publish nothing at all - which is what
         the 2024 03 13 note here suspected, and it was right.  nexus-staging-maven-plugin
         defers all uploading to the end of the reactor: each module locally stages its
         artifacts and logs "Execution skipped to the last project...", and the last project
         with the mojo in execution then performs the upload, logging "Performing remote
         staging...".  But skipNexusStagingDeployMojo is the first thing
         DeployMojo.execute() tests, and it returns immediately - whereas
         isThisLastProjectWithThisMojoInExecution() decides "last" from which projects have
         the mojo bound, not from whether it is skipped.  So -samples would still count as
         the last project, yet return before uploading anything, and -core would go nowhere.

         -samples is last because both it and -core-tests depend on -core and so cannot
         precede it; reordering the modules just moves the problem to whichever of the two
         ends up last.  Hence -pl: with only -core in the reactor it is the last (and only)
         project with the mojo, so the upload happens, and the other two never take part.

         Whatever you run, confirm "Performing remote staging..." appears in the log.
         Without it, nothing reached Central, BUILD SUCCESS notwithstanding. -->

